        "entry_date": "2026-04-22",
        "title": "Morning, paint, the long bench",
        "notes": "# Morning, paint, the long bench\n\nUp before the light. Coffee, then sketching the boats from memory before they wake up.\n\nThe new ochre is too warm — needs a bit of payne's grey to keep it from looking like dessert. Note for next time: mix on the palette, not in the cup.\n\n## Afternoon\n\nWalked to the long bench at the breakwater. Two herons, then nothing for forty-five minutes, then a seal. Wrote 800 words about it that I'm not sure I'll keep.\n\n- [x] Stretch\n- [x] First pass on the seal piece\n- [ ] Re-read it tomorrow before deciding\n- [ ] Clean brushes\n",
        "todo_list": {
          "enabled": true,
          "hide_completed": false,
          "items": [
            { "id": "018f9f01-0001-7000-8000-000000000001", "content": "Stretch", "completed": true, "position": 1024, "updated_at": "2026-04-22T07:18:00.000Z" },
